\viewkind4\pard\cf1\fs32\b Aggregate without extra coverage\b0\fs22\par\par
\pard\sa120 Exact aggregation combines blocks without adding addresses. A covering supernet may also include addresses that were not in the original selection.\par
\pard\sa180\sb120\b\fs28 Example: adjacent sibling networks\b0\fs22\par
\pard\li240\ri240\sa120\f1 192.168.10.0/25 + 192.168.10.128/25\par
= 192.168.10.0/24\par
Extra addresses = 0\f0\par
\pard\sa120 By contrast, the smallest single prefix covering \f1 192.168.10.0/26\f0  and \f1 192.168.10.128/26\f0  is a /24. That covering block includes 128 additional addresses. Keep the two /26s for an exact result.\par
\pard\sa120 Online reference: \cf2\ul CIDR aggregation\ul0\cf1  (online: \cf2\ul https://www.rfc-editor.org/info/rfc4632/\ul0\cf1 )\par
